       (24 px top padding) and the track adds another 18 px before the
       first row of tiles, so a positive `top` smaller than ~42 px makes
       the button overlap the top edge of row 1 (which lifts on tilt to
       a few px above the row baseline). Negative top positions the
       button into the section's padding zone, well above any tile. */
    top: -8px;
    right: 12px;
    z-index: 6;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--text);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      background-color 200ms var(--ease-out),
      border-color 200ms var(--ease-out),
      color 200ms var(--ease-out);
